<title>USA: Adolph Coors Q3 shr $0.49 vs $0.43.</title>
<headline>Adolph Coors Q3 shr $0.49 vs $0.43.</headline>
<dateline>GOLDEN, Colo. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			  1995</p>
<p> Shr			 $ 0.49		   $ 0.43</p>
<p> Net			 18,675		   16,492</p>
<p> Sales		    453,500		  455,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  38,018		   38,115</p>
<p>		 9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		    $    1.04		   $ 0.97</p>
<p> Net			 39,464		   37,019</p>
<p> Sales		  1,324,668		1,261,185</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  38,014		   38,250</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call Mean estimate $0.52 per share.  </p>
<p>Company Full name is Adolph Coors Co.</p>
<p>Sales are after beer excise taxes.</p>
<p>Q3 1996 includes a net special credit totaling $6.7 million pretax, or $4.1 million or $0.11 per share after tax, related to a Molson Cos Ltd payment of $4.8 million related to royalties due Coors, as well as $1.9 million of income resulting from the continuing effect of changes in payroll-related practices last year.</p>
